let's talk about uh deceptive headlines  that can be written to achieve political  goals i hope that this segment is a good  snapshot of how headlines can be used to  distort and to influence and to  um push a particular narrative that may  be interesting to one media outlet  versus another so what happened well joe  biden was recently asked during his  current trip to asia  about chinese aggression towards taiwan  now that's a legitimate issue we've  talked about it on this program will  china see the chaos of what's happening  in ukraine thanks to the russian  invasion as maybe an opening in which  they could make a military move against  taiwan so china taiwan that's the issue  it's a real issue it's a legitimate  issue president joe biden was asked  about it and joe biden confirmed  if china invaded taiwan  um the u.s would intervene and that's  been american policy for a long time so  let's look at the actual question and  answer this is the source material  for the topic and the subsequent  headlines we're going to look at you  didn't want to get involved in the  ukraine conflict militarily for obvious  reasons are you willing to get involved  militarily to defend taiwan if it comes  to that yes  you are  that's the commitment we made okay so  that's not news it's there's nothing  there that's actually newsworthy  there's something called the one china  policy  you can agree with the one china policy  or you can disagree with it but the  policy has been dating all the way back  to 1979 it was first started uh stated  in 1972 the u.s acknowledges that china  on either side of the taiwan strait  maintain there is  but one china and that taiwan is a part  of china that's the united states  position  now in 2016 donald trump said the u.s  isn't necessarily bound by the one china  policy and lots of people said oh my  goodness trump is trying to change the  one china policy but then in a phone  call in 2017 that trump had with  xi jinping they talked about a number of  different things and trump agreed at the  request of president xi to honor the one  china policy okay so we have that  we also have the taiwan relations act  from 1979 and we have the six assurances  as they're called that reagan gave to  taiwan in 1982  which say that if taiwan violates the  principles the u.s  uh uh believes in  um  or if a rather if china violates the  principles that the u.s believes in the  u.s would help taiwan to defend itself  um if china were to invade the united  states would help taiwan in that  situation so this has been policy for a  really long time so biden is asked  during the press conference well if uh  china attacks would the u.s help defend  taiwan and the united states president  says yes that's the commitment we made  it's not news biden is essentially  saying  the stuff we've agreed to  for the last 40 years  we're going to abide by it that's it  that's the story  check out how every news corporation  media outlet covered it and by me by  news corp we mean fox fox business wall  street journal the wall street journal  titled their article  biden says u.s would intervene  militarily if china invaded taiwan fox  news says u.s military will defend  taiwan if it comes to that biden says  fox business segment  says biden says u.s will intervene if  china invades taiwan now again  it's not about these headlines being  literally false it's the fact that  they're being written specifically to  further the idea of biden's out there  looking for wars biden's out there  looking for military conflict and it was  trump who was keeping us out of wars  this has been the narrative in the  george w bush era the right loved war  they loved spreading democracy and all  of this different stuff and then trump  came in and trump said the iraq war was  a bad idea even though previously trump  had said i would have gone into iraq  doesn't matter trump came in and said  iraq was bad which is true uh just he's  a hypocrite on it and he said hillary  will get us into wars but i won't i'm  going to keep us out of wars and get us  out of more places  and then the claim made about joe biden  was biden's going to get us into wars  biden's bloodthirsty biden's war hungry  even though there was no such evidence  of that  and so  they want to write headlines that will  further that and most of the fox  audience probably doesn't realize most  of the wall street journal audience  doesn't realize the u.s has previously  said  we would help to defend taiwan in such a  case biden's not  treading new ground here biden's not  changing policy he's not announcing new  policy but the story that fox wants to  tell is here's biden once again looking  for military problems so they'll say  look at biden wanting to intervene  look at biden wanting to interject and  inject the military the truth is biden's  saying i'm not changing the 40-year  policy that we've had now comparatively  reuters had a more straightforward  headline for the story reuters called it  no change in u.s policy towards taiwan  says white house official now it's not  only fox opting for the more salacious  headlines most of them do it cnn had a  similar one but it's at least more fair  cnn's headline was biden says u.s would  respond militarily if china attacked  taiwan  but white house insists there's no  policy change and indeed there isn't so  it's really important to understand  how to research these things directly if  you were uh to google  one china policy  six assurances to taiwan u.s  relationship to china and taiwan you  would realize there's not a newsworthy  element here joe biden is just saying  like yeah this is the policy and we're  going to stick to the policy the story  is biden doesn't unilaterally change  anything when it comes to china and  taiwan that doesn't really make  for a very exciting headline so that's  the  genesis the oranges for lack of a better  term  of a bunch of these headlines and  hopefully instructive in understanding  how these narratives can be woven
 

